WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.338
NULLIF compares two expressions When they are equal
it returns NULL otherwise

00:00:05.362 --> 00:00:10.100
it returns the first expression A useful
text-cleaning pattern is NULLIF of

00:00:10.125 --> 00:00:15.175
trimmed text and an empty string BTRIM removes
surrounding whitespace and NULLIF

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.012
converts the empty result to NULL This gives several
representations of no

00:00:20.038 --> 00:00:26.362
usable text one consistent missing-value state Run
the query and compare original_email

00:00:26.388 --> 00:00:31.938
with normalized_email Normal email values remain
unchanged while empty

00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:37.362
or whitespace-only text becomes NULL This small
transformation makes later IS NULL

00:00:37.375 --> 00:00:39.575
and COALESCE logic easier to reason about
